<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-April non-CIS oil, product exports rise.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-April non-CIS oil, product exports rise.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia exported 34.84 million tonnes (2.09 million barrels per day) of oil to countries outside the non-Commonwealth of Independent States in the first four months of 1997, up 11 percent year-on-year, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Non-CIS oil product exports jumped 31 percent in January-April this year to 17.67 million tonnes against 13.48 million tonnes during the same period in 1996.</p>
<p>Natural gas exports fell slightly to 43.5 billion cubic metres (bcm) in the first four months of the year, two percent down from year-ago levels of 44.2 bcm, Interfax news agency quoted the committee as saying.</p>
<p>The committee gave the following data for energy exports.</p>
<p>	    RUSSIAN JAN-APRIL 1997 NON-CIS ENERGY EXPORTS</p>
<p>				Jan-April	 Jan-April	 pct</p>
<p>				  1997		1996	  change</p>
<p> Crude oil (million T)     34.84	     31.48	    +11</p>
<p> Oil products (million T)  17.67	     13.48	    +31</p>
<p> Natural gas (bcm)	   43.50	     44.20	     -2</p>
<p>Electricity</p>
<p>  (bln kilowatt hours)	2.16		3.28	    -34</p>
